<title>USA: RESEARCH ALERT - Endesa raised.</title>
<headline>RESEARCH ALERT - Endesa raised.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-05-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>ING Barings analyst Pablo Salcedo has raised his rating for Chilean power company Empresa Nacional de Electricidad SA, or Endesa, to buy from hold.</p>
<p>In a May 21 report, he wrote, &quot;With indications that rainfall will be normal in the winter of 1997, we believe that 1998 will be a year of outstanding earnings growth for Endesa and based on this we are upgrading the stock.&quot;</p>
<p>He raised his 1997 estimate for earnings per American Depositary Receipt (EPADR) 18.8 percent to $1.20. He raised his 1998 estimate for EPADR 52.4 percent to $1.89.</p>
<p>ADRs in the company were off 3/8 to 20.</p>
<p>((--Ian Simpson, Wall Street desk, (212) 859-1879))</p>
